  "id": "budget-n94s",
  "title": "Categorize: a transaction whose category is later removed returns to the queue (owner decision); skipped rows stay out",
  "description": "Owner decision 2026-11-24 (Inbox thread): 'Cleared rows come back'. Today an accepted transaction keeps its categorize_decisions row forever, so if the user later removes its category by hand it is uncategorized but hidden from the Categorize queue, excluded from counts, refused by accept (200 accepted:0 or 409) and by skip, and never re-classified. Wanted: when a transaction with an ACCEPT decision has no category any more, it is back in the queue with its earlier suggestions pending again, counted, acceptable and skippable, and a candidate for the engine. A SKIP decision is unchanged: the row stays out of the queue and the engine never looks at it. See review-edxg-2.md F3 (attached to budget-edxg) and api/src/categorize/{decision-store,queue-store,store}.ts.",
